							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<b><span style="color: Red;">group_01_without_force_to_kill</span></b> stands near uber_mob_01&#039;s un-aggro&#039;d.<br /><b><span style="color: Blue;">group_02_with_force_to_kill</span></b> starts to watch patiently..<br />[.33 seconds later]<br /><b><span style="color: Blue;">group_02_with_force_to_kill</span></b> pulls uber_mob_01 and wins.<br /><b><span style="color: Red;">group_01_without_force_to_kill</span></b> sobs<br /><br />Time (in seconds) = Desireability * Spawn Time / Patience<br /><br />We will base desireability on a 1-10pt scale.&nbsp; 1 being high, 10 being low.&nbsp; <br />spawn time will be based on a 1-10pt scale.&nbsp; 10 being a short spawn time, and 1 being a LONG spawn time.<br />Patience is based on a 1-3pt scale.&nbsp; 1= patient.&nbsp; 2= patient enough.&nbsp; 3= impatient.<br /><br />So if you have a HIGH desireability of 1 on a 1-pt long spawn time with a patience level of 3.. <br /><br />Time = 1*1/3 = .33seconds (roughly translated to as soon as they are in range to fire an arrow or cast a spell)<br /><br />Now lets look at a different scenario.. with Desireability being 10 and spawn time being 10 with a patience level of 1.<br /><br />TIme = 10*10/1 = 1min 40seconds.&nbsp; (which is a lot to ask for)<br /><br />___________________________<br /><br />anyone who actually read that-- I am sorry for taking 5minutes of your life.&nbsp; 
						</td>
